    {
      "file": "2d67f5da1d85bc71.m4a",
      "voice": "piper:en_US-lessac-high",
      "locale": "en",
      "words": "Cross a tall pea plant with a short one, and every child is tall. Cross two of those children, and a short one comes back. The genes show why.",
      "seconds": 8.696,
      "boards": [
        "566358ffc0aab064"
      ]
    },
    {
      "file": "4593bfe0b6dcaa75.m4a",
      "voice": "piper:en_US-lessac-high",
      "locale": "en",
      "words": "Far away, it's small and upside down. Closer, it grows. Inside the focus, it flips the right way up: your face in a spoon.",
      "seconds": 8.278,
      "boards": [
        "4988bd28853e932a"
      ]
    },
    {
      "file": "e6909a9b4d75bdb0.m4a",
      "voice": "piper:en_US-lessac-high",
      "locale": "en",
      "words": "I'm a volunteer teacher. Many of my students were falling behind, and I wanted to know why. I found three reasons.",
      "seconds": 6.618,
      "boards": [
        "b21fad562b8b0507"
      ]
    },
    {
      "file": "86058d6fcc45a05c.m4a",
      "voice": "piper:en_US-lessac-high",
      "locale": "en",
      "words": "In a textbook, a concave mirror is a table of six rows to memorise. In Chalk, you move the candle, and watch its image.",
      "seconds": 7.442,
      "boards": [
        "4988bd28853e932a"
      ]
    },
    {
      "file": "973caf787d0956bb.m4a",
      "voice": "piper:en_US-lessac-high",
